From: Camera firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] http: check duplicate Content-Length without Transfer-Encoding

The short-circuit AND skipped evhttp_find_unique_header when there was no
Transfer-Encoding header. dup_cl therefore remained zero even for conflicting
Content-Length values, bypassing the existing intended rejection policy.
Evaluate the uniqueness check first and preserve the existing TE/CL rejection.

Five duplicate-length HTTP regressions return 200 before this correction and
400 afterward; ordinary length/chunked requests remain accepted. This local
correction is additional framing hardening, not a claim to close every URI
decoder condition in CVE-2026-63385. No new CVE identifier is assigned here.

Upstream-Status: Pending [local correction; not submitted upstream]
Reference: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/security/advisories/GHSA-jcwh-pvf2-73p2
Reference: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/blob/release-2.1.13-stable/http.c

--- a/http.c
+++ b/http.c
@@ -2265,8 +2265,8 @@
 	int is_chunked = 0;
 	int dup_cl = 0;
 
-	if (evhttp_find_header(headers, "Transfer-Encoding") != NULL &&
-	    evhttp_find_unique_header(headers, "Content-Length", &dup_cl) != NULL) {
+	if (evhttp_find_unique_header(headers, "Content-Length", &dup_cl) != NULL &&
+	    evhttp_find_header(headers, "Transfer-Encoding") != NULL) {
 		/* Both TE and CL were present: Not allowed. */
 		return -1;
 	}
